      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day by prescription). That much raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), often used for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I'll then enter it as written. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
